/-!
# Stage-three action boundary as a root-dependent coordinate

The actual prime-three generator acts on the identity basis of the common
prime-exponent carrier.  Its source boundary is literally the existing
prime-exponent receipt boundary.  Under the joint arithmetic--Mellin
measurement, the arithmetic coordinate cancels while the Mellin coordinate
is the installed retained incidence.  Adding the existing centered trace
recovers the installed root phase.

This is the cross-coordinate boundary generated by the common action itself.
The exact existing source-boundary trace which owns this coordinate is bound
at the receipt-root consumer; this file does not manufacture a second event.
It does not assert that the retained incidence vanishes.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 3000000

namespace SaturationMonoid.ResponsibilityLifecycle.LivingLawEvolution.ConstructiveRoot
namespace NoIslandNoMagic.CanonicalRiemann.AllPlace.WeilQuadratic.Runtime
